UPDATE companies SET description='Dusenbery''s Inc. has operated in Aztec, New Mexico, since 1937. The business serves the Four-Corners region and is run by members of the Dusenbery family — Bob, Bill, Jimmy, and Kent Dusenbery — along with Sheri Thrap and Dennis Hamilton. The company began as a local supplier and has maintained a community-focused approach for over eight decades.

The company functions as a distributor and retailer of trailers and automotive parts. Its trailer lineup includes brands such as Big-Tex, Aluma, Pace/Look, Wells Cargo, and 7 Sons. On the automotive side, it stocks CarQuest parts and accessories. The shop provides walk-in sales and product selection assistance for both trailer and vehicle maintenance needs.

