UPDATE companies SET description='Armed with a manual mill, saw, manual lathe, and surface grinder, they started building molds and machining parts. The company relocated to Kearney in 1995, constructing a 7,250-square-foot facility, and added a 4,500-square-foot expansion in 2006. In October 2019, Iowa Mold & Engineering of Belle Plaine, Iowa, acquired the business, citing the skilled workforce and diverse customer base.

The company’s core business is designing and building plastic injection molds, including single-cavity, multi-cavity, multi-core-pull, hot-runner, automatic-unscrewing, and large molds for presses up to 1,500 tons. Beyond moldmaking, Dyna Tool & Mold offers custom precision machining, wire EDM, gun drilling, tool and die work, prototyping, and a full mold repair and maintenance service.

The acquisition by Iowa Mold & Engineering was intended to broaden the combined companies’ reach and efficiency within the tooling and molding industry.

