UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Salem, Massachusetts, Electronic Parts Exchange (EPE) operates as a specialist in excess electronic component recovery. The company serves original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), electronics manufacturing services (EMS) providers, and global supply chains.

EPE converts idle inventory into working capital through consignment or buyout programs, secure authorized remarketing, ESG circular reporting, and lifecycle obsolescence management. A proprietary ClearView platform tracks quotes, sales activity, balances, and recovery performance. The company also provides quality testing services including documentation inspection, external visual inspection, X-ray inspection (X6600/X6600B), solderability testing (MUST System 3), decapsulation (JetEtch), and Keyence microscopy up to 6000× magnification.

Customers span automotive, aviation/military, and medical sectors. The aviation and military segment is supported by AS9120B:2016 certification and DOD-certified test facilities. Medical clients receive semiconductors and LCDs sourced through strict vendor screening and quality control.

The company emphasizes a transparent recovery process, certified compliance (ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001, ISO 45001, AS9120B:2016), global resale reach, and consignment strategies that often outperform liquidation. Its quality system is AS6081 compliant for counterfeit detection, with rigorous external visual inspection on all incoming and outgoing shipments.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001','ISO 45001','AS9120B:2016','AS6081 compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Excess inventory recovery (consignment and buyout)", "Secure authorized remarketing", "ESG circular reporting", "Lifecycle obsolescence management", "ClearView platform for inventory tracking", "Documentation inspection", "External visual inspection", "Remarking and resurfacing testing (scrape test, solvent test)", "X-ray inspection (X6600/X6600B)", "Solderability testing (MUST System 3)", "Decapsulation (JetEtch system)", "Keyence microscopy (20\u20136000\u00d7)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aviation/Military", "Medical"], "materials": ["Semiconductors", "LCDs", "Electronic components"], "equipment": ["X6600/X6600B X-ray inspection system", "MUST System 3 solderability tester", "JetEtch decapsulation system", "Keyence microscope"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Transparent recovery process with real-time ClearView platform tracking", "Certified compliance: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001, ISO 45001, AS9120B:2016", "Global resale reach to qualified buyers worldwide", "Consignment strategies that often outperform liquidation", "AS6081 compliant counterfeit detection program"], "facts_used": ["Location: Salem, Massachusetts -> db", "Business description: excess electronic component recovery for OEMs/EMS -> /", "Proprietary ClearView platform for tracking -> /", "Services: consignment, buyout, authorized remarketing, ESG reporting, obsolescence management -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, 14001, 45001, AS9120 -> /quality", "AS6081 compliant for counterfeit