UPDATE companies SET description='EcoGen America is headquartered in Camden, Delaware, and was founded in 2016 by Trevor Guilday. The company began as a regional effort to connect homeowners with local solar installers and expanded nationwide by 2022 to cover all 50 states, Washington, D.C., and Puerto Rico. In 2025 the platform was completely rebuilt with a homeowner-first brand, strict verification frameworks, and updated data infrastructure. Leadership includes CEO Dean Mahmoud, who has worked in residential solar since 2021, and a core team overseeing data analytics, partnerships, technology, and content.

The company operates an independent solar education and research platform. It publishes the EcoGen Solar Cost Index, a state-level price benchmark built on Department of Energy laboratory benchmarks, Bureau of Labor Statistics wage data, Energy Information Administration electricity-use figures, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory transacted-price data. The index is calibrated against current marketplace quotes and proprietary cost modeling. EcoGen also maintains a verified installer network; partners must hold an active state license, demonstrate installation activity in the state, and offer a workmanship warranty covering roof penetrations. The company processes quote requests from homeowners and earns referral fees from partner installers, while keeping editorial content independent of advertising relationships.

EcoGen serves residential homeowners exploring solar adoption across the United States. Its guides address system pricing, federal and state incentives, financing options, and installer selection. The platform’s matching service connects homeowners with solar providers in their area; as of September 2026 the network included six commercial partners. The company’s data and methodology are referenced by contributing experts in solar policy, tax credits, and clean energy journalism.

EcoGen was created to close a transparency gap in the solar industry, where homeowners faced high-pressure sales tactics without reliable, unbiased data. The founder’s stated goal is to provide free educational resources, up-to-date pricing insights, and personalized quote comparisons so that homeowners know exactly what they are buying before signing a contract. The company emphasizes public data sources, a published verification methodology, and a revenue model that does not influence editorial recommendations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar cost benchmarking and price estimation", "Installer verification and vetting", "Homeowner lead generation and quote matching", "Solar incentive and tax credit research", "Educational content publishing and guide production", "Proprietary solar cost modeling and data analytics"], "industries": ["Residential solar energy", "Renewable energy education", "Solar installer referral services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2016 by Trevor Guilday -> /about-us", "CEO Dean Mahmoud, in residential solar since 2021 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Camden, Delaware -> db", "Nationwide expansion to 50 states + DC + Puerto Rico in 2022 -> /about-us", "Platform rebuilt in 2025 with homeowner-first brand -> /about-us", "25,000+ quote requests processed -> /about-us", "6 current commercial partners as of September 24, 2026 -> /about-us", "EcoGen Solar Cost Index methodology (DOE, BLS, EIA, Berkeley Lab) -> /about-us", "EcoGen Verified Installer three-check criteria -> /about-us and /", "Referral fee revenue model, editorial independence -> /about-us and /", "Team members: Trevor Guilday, Dean Mahmoud, Dean Mazariegos, Ahmed Rawaf, James Kahle -> /about-us", "Contributing experts: Chris Meehan, Anders Alexander, Layton Smith Sr. -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "EcoGen America is an independent solar education platform built to simplify the transition to renewable energy. We translate complex pricing, incentives, and equipment options into clear, practical guidance you can trust.", "founded_year": "2016", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ecogen-america' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ecotex Healthcare Linen Service, headquartered in Albuquerque, New Mexico, traces its roots to 1959 when Eldon and Ruth Bartsch opened Southgate Cleaners, a small local cleaning service. The company remains privately owned and family-led, now under the third generation of the Bartsch family, with Bryan Bartsch serving as president and CEO.

The company operates multiple regional laundry facilities, including what it describes as the largest healthcare laundry plant in North America. With a workforce of more than 1,700 employees, Ecotex processes over one million pieces of hygienically clean healthcare linen daily. Its services span healthcare laundering, surgical sterilization, linen management, and on-site linen distribution, supported by highly automated tunnel washing systems and environmentally friendly practices such as water conservation and eco-friendly detergents.

Ecotex serves hospitals, long-term care facilities, and medical centers across Canada and North America. Its customer base includes large healthcare systems that rely on the company for patient apparel, bedding, surgical linens, PPE, scrubs, and infection-control textiles.

The company emphasizes its family ownership as a differentiator, stating it enables quick decision-making, long-term reinvestment, and direct issue resolution without layers of approval. Ecotex also highlights its Hygienically Clean and Clean Green certifications, along with HLAC accreditation, as markers of its commitment to quality and sustainability.', certifications=ARRAY['Hygienically Clean','Clean Green®','HLAC accreditation']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Healthcare linen and laundry services", "Surgical sterilization", "Linen management", "On-site linen distribution", "Reusable textile supply (patient gowns, bedding, surgical linens, PPE, scrubs)", "Automated tunnel washing", "Water conservation systems", "Energy conservation systems", "Environmentally friendly detergent use"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Hospitals", "Long-term care facilities", "Medical facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Highly automated tunnel washing system"], "volume": "Over 1,000,000 pieces daily", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, third-generation leadership enabling rapid decision-making", "Largest healthcare laundry plant in North America", "Hygienically Clean and Clean Green certified with HLAC accreditation", "Processes over one million linen pieces daily across multiple regional facilities", "Operates highly automated tunnel washing systems with water and energy conservation"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Founded 1959 by Eldon and Ruth Bartsch -> /about-us", "Family-owned, third-generation Bartsch family leadership -> /about-us", "Bryan Bartsch President and CEO -> /about-us", "More than 1,700 employees -> /, /about-us", "Largest healthcare laundry plant in North America -> /", "Over one million pieces of hygienically clean linen daily -> /, /about-us", "Services: healthcare laundering, surgical sterilization, linen management, on-site distribution -> /about-us", "Highly automated tunnel washing sy