UPDATE companies SET description='Edesia Nutrition was founded in 2010 in North Kingstown, Rhode Island, by Navyn Salem, who serves as CEO. The organization was named after the Roman goddess of food and began after Salem was inspired by a 60 Minutes segment on Plumpy''Nut''s impact in Niger.

The company produces a full range of ready-to-use therapeutic foods (RUTF) to treat and prevent malnutrition. Its Rhode Island factory manufactures up to 88 million pounds of product annually, using ingredients sourced from 17 U.S. states.

Edesia serves humanitarian organizations, governments, and global health partners, delivering to communities in crisis across more than 65 countries. The company also coordinates last-mile logistics by land, air, and sea.

