UPDATE companies SET description='The Electric Barn, Inc. was founded in 1990 in North Hampton, New Hampshire, by a former electrical contractor and master electrician who continues to run the business. He established the company after recognizing a need for competitively priced, safe, and reliable obsolete electrical equipment to gain an edge over competitors.

The company operates a 60,000-square-foot warehouse and an in-house reconditioning and testing facility. It buys, sells, and trades new, used, and reconditioned electrical equipment — including circuit breakers, switchgear, and motor controls — and provides demolition assistance, salvage, and recycling services.

The firm serves buyers who need quick turnaround on replacement parts, as well as sellers looking to liquidate surplus or decommissioned electrical assets.

