UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Integration Inc. operates from Feasterville, Pennsylvania, where it has built a reputation over more than two decades as a women-led, family-oriented electronics manufacturer. The company does not publish a specific founding year, but its leadership emphasizes a personal sense of ownership and long-term commitment to customers.

The company provides end-to-end electronics manufacturing services, including PCB assembly (surface-mount, through-hole, and mixed-technology), box build and electro-mechanical assembly, PCB fabrication, conformal coating, selective soldering, and cable assembly. Its facility runs automated stencil printers, pick-and-place machines, reflow ovens, selective soldering systems, and rework stations, supporting both leaded and lead-free processes. Programs span rapid prototyping through low- and high-volume production, with engineering review, inspection, and functional testing integrated into the workflow.

Electronic Integration serves OEMs across eight core market segments: automation, communications, energy, automotive, wearable technology, consumer electronics, LED lighting, and healthcare. The company also lists medical, industrial, and telecom customers, and its quality system is geared toward mission-critical applications requiring IPC-A-610 Class 2 and Class 3 workmanship.

The firm says its differentiation lies in a culture guided by family values and female leadership, which it says translates into accountability and continuity. Quality is described as embedded throughout the manufacturing flow—from design-for-manufacturability reviews to final verification—rather than confined to a final inspection gate. The company also highlights a 24-hour quote response time and program management that coordinates engineering, materials, production, and delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC-A-610 Class 2','IPC-A-610 Class 3','IPC-6012','RoHS','REACH','Conflict Materials compliance','NSF-ISR Certificate of Registration']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly (SMT, through-hole, mixed-technology)", "Box build & electro-mechanical assembly", "PCB fabrication", "Conformal coating", "Selective soldering", "Cable assembly", "Rapid prototyping", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) review", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "Functional testing", "Program management", "Supply chain management", "Engineering review", "Project coordination", "Production planning", "Quality coordination", "Schedule management", "Customer communication"], "industries": ["Automation", "Communications", "Energy", "Automotive", "Wearable technology", "Consumer electronics", "LED lighting", "Healthcare", "Medical", "Industrial", "Telecom"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Stencil printers", "Surface mount pick-and-place machines", "Reflow ovens", "Selective soldering machines", "Rework stations", "Automated optical inspection (AOI) equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "24-hour quote response", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Women-led, family-oriented ownership model", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "IPC-A-610 Class 2/3 and IPC-6012 compliant manufacturing", "Automated SMT, selective soldering, and inspection equipment", "Prototype-to-production volume flexibility with 24-hour quote respon