UPDATE companies SET description='EnaChip Inc. is based in Rocky Hill, New Jersey. The company develops and manufactures magnetics for high-frequency power conversion, with a focus on AI data center infrastructure.

The company produces bespoke magnetics—including multilayer inductors and wafer-level arrays—that enable vertical power delivery for 800V DC architectures. Its fabrication process uses electroplating on standard semiconductor equipment to create thick copper planar windings and high-flux-density cores, achieving low DC resistance and efficient switching above 10 MHz. Devices range from single ~1 mm components to wafer-level arrays, integrating with GaN and advanced silicon switches.

EnaChip targets operators and designers of AI data centers and high-performance computing systems where power delivery losses are a primary constraint. Its technology addresses the last-centimeter conversion and routing losses between voltage regulators and processor dies. The company also lists energy harvesting and energy conversion among its served markets.

EnaChip states that its electroplated core stacks cut manufacturing time dramatically and that its parts drop into any level of a design stack—board, package, or die. The company emphasizes that power delivery should enable performance rather than limit it, positioning its magnetics as a way to unlock the capabilities of next-generation switches.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrochemical wafer fabrication", "Wafer-aligned fabrication", "Field-to-electrical conversion", "Multilayer magnetics fabrication", "Electroplating on standard semiconductor equipment", "Vertical power delivery design", "IVR and TLVR design", "Custom geometry, feature set, and layer count manufacturing", "Wafer-level array production", "Single device fabrication (~1 mm)", "High-frequency switch integration (GaN, advanced silicon)", "Power conversion magnetics design"], "industries": ["AI data centers", "High-performance computing", "Power conversion", "Energy harvesting", "Energy conversion"], "materials": ["High-flux-density magnetic materials", "Low-loss magnetic materials", "Copper", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)", "Silicon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Electroplating on standard semiconductor equipment reduces manufacturing time", "Multilayer magnetics suppress core loss at high switching frequencies (>10 MHz)", "Parts integrate at board, package, or die level", "Vertical power delivery for 800V DC architectures", "Integration with GaN and advanced silicon switches"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Rocky Hill, New Jersey -> db", "Makes magnetics for AI data center power conversion -> page \"/\"", "Uses electroplating on standard semiconductor equipment -> page \"/\"", "Offers wafer-level array and single device ~1mm -> page \"/\"", "Targets vertical power delivery for 800V DC architectures -> page \"/\"", "Collaborates with Singh Center at UPenn -> page \"/\"", "Capabilities include electrochemical wafer fabrication and wafer-aligned fabrication -> db", "Industries served include energy harvesting and energy conversion -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Electroplating on standard semiconductor equipment cuts manufacturing time dramatically, and our parts drop into any level of your design stack.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='enachip-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Encompass Manufacturing operates from Cookeville, Tennessee, where it was founded over 35 years ago by Ricky Sherrell as Putnam County Plastic Molding. The company is certified as a Women''s Business Enterprise through WBENC and is now led by President Samantha Sherrell, with Ricky Sherrell serving as vice president.

The firm specializes in plastic injection molding supported by a full-service tool shop and a range of secondary operations including sonic welding, hot stamping, screen printing, pad printing, insert molding, vibratory welding, drilling, and assembly. Its press lineup spans 125 to 1,214 tons, enabling production of complex components from engineering-grade resins. A proprietary Mattec/MVP system provides real-time scheduling, inventory tracking, and preventive maintenance data, while an on-site metrology lab offers calibration and inspection services.

Customers range from small startups to major automotive suppliers worldwide. The company''s quality system, certified to ISO 9001, incorporates Advanced Product Quality Planning (APQP), Production Part Approval Process (PPAP), and full traceability from raw material to final assembly.

