UPDATE companies SET description='Ennis Fine Furniture was founded in 1946 in Boise, Idaho, when World War II veteran Cecil Ennis and his brother-in-law purchased a former horse stable at 23rd Street and Fairview Avenue and converted it into a furniture and appliance store. The business has remained family-owned for nearly eight decades, passing from Cecil to his son Dick Ennis in 1968 and now to the third generation—grandchildren Rick, Jeff, and Cathy—who continue to operate the company today.

The retailer operates two showrooms, in Boise and Spokane, Washington, offering living-room, bedroom, and dining-room collections that include sofas, sectionals, chairs, tables, beds, dressers, and cabinetry. Ennis Fine Furniture positions itself as a destination for semi-custom and luxury furnishings, providing design consultation to help clients select finishes, stains, and configurations. The company also handles delivery, installation, and haul-away of old furniture.

Its customer base consists primarily of residential homeowners throughout the Pacific Northwest. Testimonials cite purchases ranging from dining tables and floor lamps to complete family-room sets, with clients emphasizing the personalized attention from named design consultants such as John Ambrose, Mary Ann, and Patti.

The company attributes its longevity to its family-legacy values—trust, loyalty, and a personalized experience—rather than mass-market trends. As the ownership states, the goal is not only to provide handcrafted furniture but to ensure every step of the journey is met with care and attention, making the purchase an investment in a piece of history and artistry.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture retail", "Design consultation", "Custom finish and stain selection", "Delivery and installation", "Haul-away service"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1946", "Semi-custom and luxury furnishings with design consultation", "Delivery, installation, and old-furniture haul-away", "Two showrooms serving the Northwest (Boise, ID and Spokane, WA)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 by Cecil Ennis and brother-in-law in Boise, Idaho -> /about-us", "Family-owned, now run by grandchildren Rick, Jeff, Cathy -> /about-us", "Two locations: Boise (275 S 23rd St) and Spokane (8313 N Division St) -> /about-us", "Sells living room, bedroom, dining room furniture; offers semi-custom and luxury furnishings -> /", "Provides design consultation, delivery, installation, haul-away -> /", "Customer testimonials reference purchases of dining tables, lamps, sofas, etc. -> /", "Company emphasizes family legacy, trust, personalized experience -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "started to sell furniture and appliances", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ennis-fine-furniture-boise' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Epic Welding & Mfg operates as a full-service welding and fabrication shop in West Fargo, North Dakota. The company has accumulated over 20 years of experience in the manufacturing industry, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The shop provides a range of metal fabrication services including MIG, stick, and TIG welding; CNC plasma cutting up to 1-inch mild steel; 12-foot press brake forming; plate shearing up to 1/4-inch by 10 feet; sawing capacity to 18 by 18 inches; punching and notching; sand blasting; epoxy two-part painting via an automated Pro Mix blender; and final assembly. Work volumes span from single prototypes and 1–10 piece orders up to runs of 1,000 pieces, covering small to medium production quantities.

Epic Welding serves industrial and agricultural customers, regularly building trailers, agricultural equipment, and pipe work. The company emphasizes custom, tailor-made fabrication for each job, working with aluminum, stainless steel, and mild steel to meet customer specifications.

